WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:00.900
Tonight.

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.002
Trump's tax returns

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:03.870
are now in the hands of House Democrats

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.939
on the Ways and Means Committee.

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:07.007
Look, this is a huge step.

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:07.841
It was a years

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:09.642
long battle to get these tax returns

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.011
right that no one's ever seen.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.979
They cover six years of former

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:14.381
President Trump's taxes.

00:00:14.381 --> 00:00:16.182
Information about his personal finances

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.584
is corporate entities.

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:18.752
This is crucial stuff.

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:19.185
And OUTFRONT

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:20.820
now is the Democratic Congressman, Lloyd

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.288
Doggett, the member of the House Ways

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:22.922
and Means Committee,

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.290
who our viewers know

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.992
has been talking to us about this.

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:26.726
Congressman, you know,

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:27.494
I spoke with you

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:29.429
the night that the Supreme Court

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:30.397
gave you the green light,

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:31.731
finally clearing the way

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.900
for your committee to get Trump's taxes.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.402
Here we are ten days later.

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:37.170
Your committee's got them in hand.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.371
What is the committee doing

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:39.039
with them right now?

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.208
Well, Aaron, finally, after

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:45.845
making the motion in February of 2017

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:49.549
almost five years ago,

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.517
the Ways and Means

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:51.117
chairman

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:54.387
has excess access to those returns

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:56.056
to some of the returns

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:57.891
that I was seeking at that time.

00:00:57.891 --> 00:00:59.526
We had a meeting yesterday.

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:01.861
He explained the process.

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.296
He indicated that he did

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:04.664
have access to them,

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:06.433
that he had appointed

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:09.002
some staff individuals

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:11.471
his agents to go through the returns.

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.641
And I believe that is occurring

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:15.308
right now

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:17.377
needs to occur very expeditiously

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:19.279
because we know we have only

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:20.780
a few days left

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:21.915
in which Democrats

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:23.283
would be in charge of this.

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.984
And we know how much obstruction

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:27.520
two years from congressional Republicans

00:01:27.821 --> 00:01:29.322
and then this case sat for two

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:31.357
and a half years with a

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:32.625
Trump appointed judge.

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:34.561
So finally, we have it.

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:37.764
We need to then meet in executive session

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:39.099
to hear what

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:40.233
these individuals

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.802
who've been reviewing the returns

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:45.271
find and make a determination

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:49.109
about how much if at all is made public.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:49.742
All right.

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:50.677
So I want to ask you

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:51.611
about the public part of this.

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:53.279
But first, when you say only a few days.

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:54.848
Obviously, January 3rd, right, is

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:56.549
when the gavel switches over.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:58.818
So and not many of those days

00:01:58.818 --> 00:01:59.419
are in session.

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:00.954
But when we spoke, you had said

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:02.222
you were willing to have this

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:03.456
go around the clock,

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:05.225
work on the weekends, work 40 hours

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:06.759
a day, whatever it took.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:08.595
Is that happening?

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:10.296
I'm hopeful that it is.

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:11.431
We've been provided

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:12.532
as members of the committee,

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:14.267
very few details

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:17.437
about how this exploration is occurring.

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:19.139
But I think

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:21.040
from talking with Chairman Neal,

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.442
while he's very prudent

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:24.110
about following the law

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:26.279
and protecting privacy here,

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:28.314
he knows how urgent this is.

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:30.683
And that come January 3rd,

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:32.152
he will no longer be chair,

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:34.020
unfortunately, of the committee.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.522
And that the work has to be done

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:36.489
before that.

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:38.024
And I think he recognizes

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:39.893
the responsibility to the public

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:41.161
and to our committee

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:42.428
to come up with an answer.

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:45.431
So I feel we'll have whether in-person

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:49.869
or by zoom, a meeting of our committee

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:53.339
in executive private session there.

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:54.340
We will determine

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.442
what to do with the outcome.

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:58.678
It is best to look and get the results.

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.914
But the more I learn about this case,

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:02.215
the more I'm convinced that

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:03.550
at this late moment,

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:05.752
we really do need to make all

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:07.187
or a substantial portion

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:08.721
of this available to the public.

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:09.455
So then that

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:10.456
that gets me exactly

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:11.991
what I wanted to ask you.

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:13.760
So how does that happen?

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:14.427
Because obviously,

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:15.361
you can do what you can do

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:16.329
if you can't finish it

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:17.730
or come to conclusions. Right.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.566
The best way to get it into

00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:20.800
to have it not disappear,

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.302
which it which it will. Right.

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:23.736
If Republicans take over the committee

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:24.604
and it stays in committee,

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:26.339
it is to put it in the public eye.

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:28.808
Is that going to happen or. Exactly.

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:29.842
You're exactly right,

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:31.945
because all of the Republicans

00:03:31.945 --> 00:03:33.646
who are talking about being on the ways

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:35.615
and Means Committee chairmanship

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:36.749
have already worked

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:38.551
to obstruct our access to this

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:39.452
and have made clear

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:41.020
they want to have nothing to do

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:41.487
with this.

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:43.523
Beginning on January 3rd,

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:44.824
the way it could occur

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:47.460
is in an executive private session,

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:50.463
we decide to report this to the House

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:51.631
and attach

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.299
some or all of the returns

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:56.603
or return information to that report.

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:58.304
Thereby, it could become public.

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:00.406
We'll take a vote of our committee,

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:02.575
but you could do that by January 3rd.

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:04.377
Yes, we could.

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:04.711
All right.

00:04:04.711 --> 00:04:06.346
Thank you very much, Congressman Doggett.

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:07.947
I appreciate your time tonight.

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:08.615
Thank you very much.

